This problem tests your ability to define DP states, formulate transitions, compute predecessor relationships, and reconstruct solutions. It extends the classic weighted interval scheduling problem with an additional constraint on the number of selections.

## Key Concepts
- Weighted interval scheduling with a selection cap k
- Predecessor array p[i] computed via binary search on sorted end times
- Backtracking to recover the indices of selected tasks

